Package: liblibrescrs5
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: librescrs-card-plugins (= ${binary:Version})
Description: LibreSCRS smart-card middleware runtime libraries
 LibreSCRS reads Serbian government smart cards (identity, vehicle and health)
 as well as generic ICAO eMRTD, NIST PIV and PKCS#15 cards, talking to the
 reader over PC/SC directly.
 .
 This package holds the shared libraries and the PKCS#11 provider module. The
 module is installed but not registered with p11-kit; registration is a
 separate decision and a separate package.

Package: librescrs-card-plugins
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, liblibrescrs5 (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Card plugins for the LibreSCRS middleware
 One dlopen'd plugin per card family, with the manifest that describes the
 fields each one exposes.
 .
 Without this package the libraries load and enumerate readers but recognise
 no card.

Package: librescrs-pkcs11-direct
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, liblibrescrs5 (>= ${source:Version})
Conflicts: librescrs-agent
Description: Register the LibreSCRS PKCS#11 module directly with p11-kit
 Installs the p11-kit declaration that makes PKCS#11-aware applications
 discover the LibreSCRS provider in their own process.
 .
 This is the alternative to the agent, not a companion to it. The agent
 registers a proxy that collects the PIN in its own prompter, behind an
 authorization prompt; the direct module takes the PIN inside whichever
 application loaded it. Registering both would leave one card with two
 security models and let whichever dialog the user typed into decide which one
 they got, so the two packages conflict and installing either replaces the
 other. On a machine with a desktop session the agent is the one you want.

Package: liblibrescrs-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         liblibrescrs5 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libpcsclite-dev,
         libssl-dev
Description: Development files for the LibreSCRS middleware
 Headers, linker symlinks and the CMake package configuration for building
 against LibreSCRS.
 .
 The two development dependencies are not decoration. The installed CMake
 config calls find_dependency for PCSC and for OpenSSL before it defines a
 single target, so without their headers every downstream find_package fails at
 configuration -- which is exactly how it was found.
